---
/**
 * t69 · Arrival
 *
 * The tail is not decoration. It is the mouth the voice came out of, and it
 * is the only part of a speech bubble that says which way the sound is going.
 * So the light is struck from there.
 *
 * Tone is one monotonic falloff measured from a point just past the tip of
 * the tail: deepest at the mouth, opening and brightening as it climbs
 * through the body. That makes the level lines curved and concentric about
 * the tail — tight and dark where the voice starts, wide and pale by the time
 * they reach the shoulders, which they cross symmetrically because they are
 * centred on the tail rather than on the bubble.
 *
 * It is monotonic, so there are no repeated rings and nothing here can be
 * read as a signal glyph. One continuous swell, not a diagram.
 *
 * This also settles the usual complaint about tails. Where a tail is a wedge
 * glued to a rounded rectangle, it looks glued on. Here every tone in the
 * bubble is measured *from* the tail, so the tail is where the interior comes
 * from, and body and tail share one exact outline.
 *
 * The carrier is an ordinary rounded chat bubble with a long stepped tail.
 * The face is the family's md/compact/gap-2, sitting on a plateau the swell
 * flattens into and then darkens for contrast.
 *
 * 11 tones, deep violet through to magenta.
 */
import MarkFrame from '../MarkFrame.astro';
import { facePathsAt } from '../../../data/mark';

interface Props { size?: number }
const { size = 128 } = Astro.props;
---

